further:
  - slug: dur-sharrukin
    why: The city Sargon II founded and moved the seat of government to in 706 BC,
      ending Nimrud's run as imperial capital.
  - slug: nineveh
    why: Where Sennacherib moved the capital next — and the name Layard attached
      to the Nimrud mounds before the identification was settled.
  - slug: assur
    why: The older capital Ashurnasirpal II left behind, where Assyrian kings
      continued to be buried while their queens were interred at Calah.
