    list and no claim in the prose to attach it to, so it could not be
    carried. The sentence about Carsten Niebuhr in the "Nimrud" section breaks
    off mid-thought in the source ("Niebuhr" followed by its two references),
    so only the complete part was rewritten. The two Layard sketches of a
    Lamassu being lowered and transported, and every picture in the gallery,
